We are now improving the interactive portfolio experience inside the BlueMind Web Service website.

IMPORTANT:
- Work on the portfolio project cards and project viewer only.
- Do not redesign the Hero.
- Do not touch the backend.
- Do not add authentication.
- Do not change unrelated pages.
- Keep the current BlueMind visual identity.
- Apply this interaction system consistently to EVERY portfolio project.

The goal is to make the Selected Work section feel premium, interactive, and clearly demonstrate that every project is a real responsive website experience.

==================================================
1. PORTFOLIO CARD HOVER
==================================================

Every portfolio project card should have a strong interactive hover state.

When the user moves the mouse over a project card:

1. The entire card should lift slightly upward.
2. Add a smooth transition.
3. Blur the project preview strongly enough that the preview content becomes secondary.
4. Add a subtle darker or translucent overlay if needed so the CTA text remains readable.
5. Show a clear centered CTA in English.

Preferred CTA:

View Project

Alternative acceptable wording:
Explore Project
View Demo
Open Preview

Use ONE wording consistently across all portfolio cards.

The CTA should appear in the center of the card.

Do NOT use blue hover text.

Keep the hover style aligned with BlueMind’s black/white design language.

Suggested hover behavior:

transform: translateY(-4px)

Possible slight scale:
1.01 maximum

Transition:
approximately 220–300ms

Easing:
cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)

The animation should feel premium and controlled.

Do not use:
- bouncing
- strong zoom
- excessive shadows
- spinning
- flashy color changes

==================================================
2. BLUR EFFECT
==================================================

The preview should blur when hovered.

Use a noticeable but tasteful blur.

The visitor should still understand that a website preview exists behind the overlay, but the attention should move to:

View Project

Possible blur:
6px–10px

Use visual judgment.

Make sure the text remains sharp.

Do not blur the CTA itself.

Do not create performance-heavy effects.

==================================================
3. TOUCH DEVICES
==================================================

Hover does not exist on phones and tablets.

Therefore:

On touch devices, the project card must still clearly indicate that it is clickable.

Use one or more of:

- always-visible small “View Project” label
- visible CTA button
- subtle arrow/indicator
- tap feedback

Do NOT make the user depend on hover to discover the project.

==================================================
4. OPEN PROJECT INTERACTION
==================================================

When the visitor clicks/taps a project:

DO NOT navigate away from BlueMind.

DO NOT open a new browser tab.

DO NOT replace the current page permanently.

Open the project inside the current BlueMind website using the project viewer.

The opening animation must feel intentional.

I want the project viewer to rise FROM THE BOTTOM UP.

It should feel like a large panel/window opening over the current website.

Suggested behavior:

closed:
transform: translateY(100%)

opening:
transform: translateY(0)

Use a smooth animation.

Suggested duration:
400–550ms

Suggested easing:
cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)

The BlueMind page can remain visible underneath during the transition.

Avoid sudden appearance.

==================================================
5. CLOSING THE PROJECT VIEWER
==================================================

When the user closes the project:

Do NOT make it disappear instantly.

Reverse the opening animation.

The viewer should smoothly move DOWN and leave the screen.

Sequence:

open:
bottom → up

close:
current position → down

Only unmount the viewer after the closing animation finishes.

When closed:

Restore the user to the exact same scroll position in the BlueMind portfolio.

Do not jump to the top of the Home page.

==================================================
6. PROJECT VIEWER TOP BAR
==================================================

At the top of the opened project viewer, create a clean browser/macOS-inspired control bar.

The top bar should remain visually separate from the project website.

Include:

LEFT:
Three circular window controls

Red
Yellow
Green

Use proper macOS-style spacing and proportions.

They should look polished and intentional.

Do NOT make them huge.

Suggested behavior:

Red:
Close project viewer

Yellow:
Optional minimize/compact behavior if useful

Green:
Optional expand/fullscreen behavior if appropriate

If the yellow or green actions are not yet useful, they may remain visual controls temporarily, but the RED button should definitely work as Close.

If implementing yellow/green behavior is simple and useful:

Yellow:
temporarily reduce the preview size / minimize within viewer

Green:
toggle expanded/fullscreen preview

Do not introduce unstable complexity solely to make them functional.

